1
00:00:06,650 --> 00:00:08,471
There you are.

2
00:00:08,471 --> 00:00:10,082
Forgive me.

3
00:00:10,082 --> 00:00:14,354
I promised myself I would not say that this time.

4
00:00:17,483 --> 00:00:20,304
I remember you, champion.

5
00:00:20,304 --> 00:00:22,515
No one else does.

6
00:00:22,515 --> 00:00:24,574
Not the guards.

7
00:00:24,574 --> 00:00:26,861
Not the priestess.

8
00:00:26,861 --> 00:00:30,978
Not even the people whose lives you saved.

9
00:00:30,978 --> 00:00:32,579
But I do.

10
00:00:35,233 --> 00:00:37,105
Have we met?

11
00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:41,394
You have never met me.

12
00:00:41,394 --> 00:00:45,486
That is not quite the same as us never having met.

13
00:00:48,317 --> 00:00:50,629
You were here before.

14
00:00:50,629 --> 00:00:52,942
You broke the stones.

15
00:00:52,942 --> 00:00:55,675
You defeated the Minotaurs.

16
00:00:55,675 --> 00:00:58,128
You painted the mosaic.

17
00:00:58,128 --> 00:01:00,581
And then you were gone.

18
00:01:04,025 --> 00:01:06,617
I do not remember any of that.

19
00:01:08,775 --> 00:01:11,212
You thought it was a game.

20
00:01:11,212 --> 00:01:15,252
A place that would wait quietly until you returned.

21
00:01:15,252 --> 00:01:18,394
But the sun went down after you left.

22
00:01:18,394 --> 00:01:21,087
We still had to bury our dead.

23
00:01:24,525 --> 00:01:26,772
The stones you shattered.

24
00:01:26,772 --> 00:01:30,356
We had forgotten why our ancestors raised them.

25
00:01:30,356 --> 00:01:33,028
The creatures beneath the earth.

26
00:01:33,028 --> 00:01:38,373
We called them monsters because none of us could remember what they guarded.

27
00:01:41,233 --> 00:01:42,961
And the mosaic?

28
00:01:44,817 --> 00:01:48,926
Did anyone tell you what the picture was supposed to be?

29
00:01:48,926 --> 00:01:51,465
Or did your hands simply know?

30
00:01:54,733 --> 00:01:58,045
It was different when you first came.

31
00:01:58,045 --> 00:02:00,884
This road bent toward the sea.

32
00:02:00,884 --> 00:02:03,925
There was a tree beside the gate.

33
00:02:03,925 --> 00:02:06,763
Your shield bore another mark.

34
00:02:06,763 --> 00:02:09,061
You wore another face.

35
00:02:12,108 --> 00:02:13,981
I had a brother.

36
00:02:13,981 --> 00:02:15,987
There is no grave.

37
00:02:15,987 --> 00:02:19,664
There is no empty bed in my mother's house.

38
00:02:19,664 --> 00:02:22,205
There was never a brother.

39
00:02:22,205 --> 00:02:26,484
Except that I remember teaching him to hold a spear.

40
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:33,774
How can you remember a world that never existed?

41
00:02:36,025 --> 00:02:40,613
I was born with memories of things that had not happened.

42
00:02:40,613 --> 00:02:44,803
As a child, I thought everyone dreamed of tomorrow.

43
00:02:44,803 --> 00:02:46,864
Then tomorrow came.

44
00:02:46,864 --> 00:02:48,793
And it was wrong.

45
00:02:52,233 --> 00:02:56,418
Each time the world changes, something remains.

46
00:02:56,418 --> 00:02:58,688
A scratch in bronze.

47
00:02:58,688 --> 00:03:01,171
A name spoken in sleep.

48
00:03:01,171 --> 00:03:05,001
A color that does not belong in the stone.

49
00:03:07,650 --> 00:03:10,537
You painted that mosaic once.

50
00:03:10,537 --> 00:03:14,058
Before the mason who made it was born.

51
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:21,502
There is one figure in it that no one can explain.

52
00:03:21,502 --> 00:03:24,875
A soldier standing behind the champion.

53
00:03:24,875 --> 00:03:27,720
His face has been scraped away.

54
00:03:30,775 --> 00:03:33,572
I do not remember doing that.

55
00:03:33,572 --> 00:03:37,255
But there was stone dust beneath my nails.

56
00:03:41,108 --> 00:03:43,076
Why should I trust you?

57
00:03:45,233 --> 00:03:46,921
You should not.

58
00:03:46,921 --> 00:03:51,857
But remember what I said before someone tells you a kinder version.

59
00:03:54,608 --> 00:03:56,894
I did not come to stop you.

60
00:03:56,894 --> 00:03:59,238
I came to ask you something.

61
00:03:59,238 --> 00:04:03,165
When you finish what brought you here, before you leave

62
00:04:03,165 --> 00:04:07,208
us again, find out who told you to break the first stone.

63
00:04:10,442 --> 00:04:12,914
And if I find you here tomorrow?

64
00:04:15,358 --> 00:04:17,869
Ask me about my brother.

65
00:04:17,869 --> 00:04:22,054
If I tell you I never had one, do not follow me.
